.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH ifg-events 1  "ifg-events 0.9.1"
.SH NAME
ifg\-events \- Read the repository event log by cursor
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBifg events\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Read the repository event log by cursor
.PP
`events list` makes one plain read: the events after `\-\-since`, plus `next_cursor` to pass back on the next call. Without `\-\-since` the server returns only the current cursor, which is the starting position and not an empty result. The command never waits for new events.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
ifg\-events\-list(1)
List the events after a cursor (one read, no waiting)
.TP
ifg\-events\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
.SH VERSION
v0.9.1
